{"name":"Sphagnum Moss","hex":"#75693d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sphagnum moss","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of sphagnum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sphagnum_moss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sphagnum","blocks":[{"text":"Sphagnum is a genus of approximately 380 species of mosses, commonly known as sphagnum moss, also bog moss and quacker moss. Accumulations of Sphagnum can store water, since both living and dead plants can hold large quantities of water inside their cells; plants may hold 16 to 26 times as much water as their dry weight, depending on the species. The empty cells help retain water in drier conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Sphagnum.flexuosum.jpg/330px-Sphagnum.flexuosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphagnum","wikidata":"Q30019"},{"title":"Moss","blocks":[{"text":"Mosses are small, non-vascular flowerless plants in the taxonomic division Bryophyta sensu stricto. Bryophyta sensu lato may also refer to the parent group, bryophytes, which comprises liverworts, mosses, and hornworts. Mosses typically form dense green clumps or mats, often in damp or shady locations. The individual plants are usually composed of simple leaves that are generally only one cell thick, attached to a stem that may be branched or unbranched and has only a limited role in conducting water and nutrients. Although some species have conducting tissues, these are generally poorly developed and structurally different from similar tissue found in vascular plants. Mosses do not have seeds and after fertilisation develop sporophytes with unbranched stalks topped with single capsules containing spores. They are typically 0.2–10 cm (0.1–3.9 in) tall, though some species are much larger. Dawsonia superba, the tallest moss in the world, can grow to 60 cm (24 in) in height. There are approximately 12,000 species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Tionesta-ac-moss2.jpg/330px-Tionesta-ac-moss2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss","wikidata":"Q25347"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Sphagnum_cells.jpg/500px-Sphagnum_cells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Sphagnum_cells.jpg/1280px-Sphagnum_cells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Sphagnum_cells.jpg/500px-Sphagnum_cells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sphagnum cells","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASphagnum_cells.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Red_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG/500px-Red_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Red_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG/1280px-Red_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Red_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG/500px-Red_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red sphagnum closeup","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Sphagnum_Closeup.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sphagnum_Brown%27s_Lake_Bog.jpg/500px-Sphagnum_Brown%27s_Lake_Bog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Sphagnum_Brown%27s_Lake_Bog.jpg/1280px-Sphagnum_Brown%27s_Lake_Bog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai